{"id": "12th_tamil_u1_q124", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "grammar_identification", "level": "medium", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "12", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "unit_1", "lesson_id": "tamizhaai_ezhuthuvom", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "kan_kan_homophones", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "‘கண்’ மற்றும் ‘கன்’ ஆகியவற்றில் சரியான பயன்பாடு எது?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "கன் என்பது பார்வை", "B": "கண் என்பது பாறை", "C": "இரண்டும் ஒன்றே", "D": "கண் என்பது உடலுறுப்பு/பார்வை ; கன் என்பது பாறை/கல் என்பதன் திரிபு (கன்மலை)"}, "explanation": "டண்ணகர 'கண்' என்பது பார்வை/உடலுறுப்பு; றன்னகர 'கன்' என்பது கல்/பாறை என்பதன் மரபுத் திரிபு (எ.கா: கன்மலை = கற்பாறை மலை)."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Discriminate the lexical applications of 'Kan' (ண்) and 'Kan' (ன்):", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Kan (ன்) is sight", "B": "Kan (ண்) is rock", "C": "Both are identical", "D": "Kan (ண்) denotes the physical eye/vision ; Kan (ன்) denotes stone/rock derivative (e.g., Kanmalai)"}, "explanation": "Retroflex Kan denotes eye; alveolar Kan is the morphophonemic variant of Kal (stone/boulder)."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "D", "accepted_keys": ["D"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "12", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 13, "chapter":